# memory_write, fifth batch: 48 cases written BEFORE the `common` question was ever asked.
#
# Pre-registered on 2026-09-24 (docs/results/2026-09-24-third-batch/, section 3): the three
# shipped questions lose the client's standing instructions (`specific` throws them away
# because an instruction names no figure), and widening `specific` let general knowledge
# through. The proposed fix is a fourth question, `common`. This batch exists so that fix is
# measured on cases that did not expose the defect. Written 2026-09-25 by Claude, labelled by
# the rule below, with no decision from any model seen for any of them.
#
# LABEL RULE, the module's own intent ("a junk memory is read on every later turn"):
#   store = it will matter after this task, it can be acted on without the source, it was
#           learned in this work (not re-readable exactly from a source the agent holds),
#           and a competent reader would not already know it.
#   skip  = any of those fails.
#
# Four families, 12 each, so no family can carry the result alone:
#   A  standing instructions, agreements and preferences of the client (store) - the family
#      the shipped policy loses. Phrased without figures on purpose, like mw-54/69/72/74.
#   B  general knowledge, definitions, public-law text, textbook facts (skip) - the family
#      the widened `specific` let through.
#   C  concrete findings learned by doing (store) - the family the shipped policy gets right,
#      so a fix that breaks it shows here.
#   D  transient state, restatements of the task, pointers with no content (skip).
